$DATUM 107-06-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Beckmann Rearrangement (General Procedure) A mixture of the ketoximes (5
mM) and Silferc[18] (2.5 gm, FeCl3 content, 0.4 gm, 3 mM) was stirred in
1,2-dichloroethane at its reflux temperature. The reaction was monitored
by TLC. The mixture was filtered hot and the catalyst was washed three
times with 20 ml portion of boiling EDC. The excessive solvent was
distilled off to give anilide, which was purified by column
chromatography (4 Pet ether: 1 Ethylacetate). Combined yield of 2 & 3:
81% (Table 1, Entry 1) M.P. 162(°C)
