$DATUM 7705-08-0
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Conversion of Oximes into Amides The oxime (10mmol)
and FeCl3 (30-40mmol) were mixed in a mortar. The reaction mixture was
allowed to stand at 80-90°C for 1.5-3 h. The progress of reaction was
followed by dissolving a sample in acetone and monitoring on silica gel
plates (SIL G/UV 254 Plates). Water (15 ml) was added and the whole
extracted with chloroform (3 x 20 ml). Drying and evaporation of the
solvent gave the products in 81-95% yields which recrystallized from
n-heptane. Table 1, Entry 1, yield 82%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid state, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solvent free Beckmann rearrangement of ketoximes by anhydrous ferric
chloride
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Khodaei, M. M.; Meybodi, F. A.; Rezai, N.; Salehi, P.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2001), 31(13), 2047-2050

