$DATUM Ethyl
6-methoxy-5-methyl-2-oxo-2,3,4,5-tetrahydro-1H-benz[b]azepine-5-carboxylate
23 Aluminum trichloride (9.35 g, 70.10 mmol) was added to a solution of
(E)-ethyl
8-methoxy-1-methyl-4-(tosyloxy)imino-1,2,3,4-tetrahydronaphthalene-1-carboxylate
(7.56 g, 17.53 mmol) in dichloromethane (120 mL) at 0°C and the resulting
solution was stirred for 2.5 h, slowly warming to rt over this time and
turning deep orange. The reaction mixture was re-cooled to 0°C and
quenched by the careful addition of saturated aqueous sodium hydrogen
carbonate solution (100 mL), followed by water (100 mL) and
dichloromethane (50 mL). The resulting emulsion was acidified to pH 1
with concentrated hydrochloric acid and then extracted with
dichloromethane (3 × 100 mL). The combined extracts were washed with
water (100 mL), saturated aqueous sodium hydrogen carbonate solution (100
mL) and brine (100 mL), dried (MgSO4) and concentrated. The residue was
purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel, eluting with ethyl
acetate-light petroleum (1:2). The title compound as a yellow foam (4.05
g, 83%). Mp 112-113°C; (Found [M + Na+], 300.1198. C15H19NNaO4 + requires
300.1206); νmax (CHCl3)/cm-1 3391, 3011, 2983, 2941, 2907, 2878, 2840,
1727, 1689, 1674, 1591, 1417, 1377, 1137; δH (400 MHz; CDCl3) 7.41 (1H,
br. s), 7.16 (1H, t, J 8.2), 6.65 (1H, dd, J 8.2, 1.0), 6.47 (1H, dd, J
8.2, 1.0), 4.18 (1H, dq, J 10.7, 7.5), 4.13 (1H, dq, J 10.7, 7.5), 3.78
(3H, s), 2.93 (1H, ddd, J 15.5, 10.1, 1.3), 2.52 (1H, ddt, J 15.5, 9.4,
1.1), 2.30 (1H, ddd, J 15.1, 9.4, 1.3), 2.13 (1H, ddd, J 15.1, 10.1,
1.1), 1.54 (3H, s), 1.22 (3H, t, J 7.5); δC (100 MHz; CDCl3) 177.1 (C),
177.0 (C), 158.8 (C), 136.7 (C), 128.7 (CH), 122.4 (C), 115.4 (CH), 107.0
(CH), 60.7 (CH2), 55.5 (Me), 48.5 (C), 35.7 (CH2), 31.2 (CH2), 25.1 (Me),
14.2 (Me).
