$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Beckmann rearrangement of 6-O-allylerythromycin A 9(Z)-oximes (21).
Preparation of 6-O-allyl-8a-aza-8a-homoerythromycin A (27). To a solution
of the oxime 21 (15.86 g) in acetone (200 mL) were simultaneously added a
solution of p-TsCl (20.8 g, 0.14 moL) in acetone (340 mL) and a solution
of NaHCO3 (20.5 g, 0.28 moL) in water (340 mL) over a period of 1 hour at
a rate to keep the internal temperature below 5°C. The reaction mixture
was stirred for an additional 2 hours and then allowed to warm to room
temperature overnight. Acetone was evaporated in vacuo, the aqueous layer
was made basic (pH= 9.0) with 2M aqueous NaOH, and extracted with CH2Cl2
(2 x 150mL). The combined organic extracts were dried over K2CO3 and
evaporated in vacuo to give the crude lactam as a faintly yellow solid,
which, if appropriate, was purified by chromatography on a silica gel
column using methylene chloride-methanol-conc. ammonium hydroxide
(90:9:1.5) as eluent to give 13.16 g (83%) of 27 as colorless solids .
6-O-allyl-8a-aza-8a-homoerythromycin A (27), yield 13.16 g, 83%. Rf 0.22,
ethylacetate-n-hexane-diethylamine, 100:100:20. FAB-MS m/z 789 (MH+,
85%); IR (KBr) νmax 2974, 2936, 1746, 1646, 1320, 1053 cm-1; 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 6.23 (1H, d, 8a-CONH), 6.05 (1H, ddt, 6-OCH2CHCH2), 5.15 (1H,
dd, 6-OCH2CHCH2b), 5.08 (1H, dd, 6-OCH2CHCH2a), 4.95 (1H, dd, H-13), 4.94
(1H, d, H-1''), 4.44 (1H, d, H-1'), 4.13-4.05 (1H, m, H-8), 4.02 (1H, dd,
H-5''), 4.00-3.94 (3H, m, 6-OCH2CHCH2, H-3), 3.76 (1H, s, 11-OH), 3.71
(1H, d, H-5), 3.58-3.51 (1H, m, H-5'), 3.47 (1H, s, H-11), 3.31 (3H, s,
3''-OMe), 3.25 (1H, dd, H-2'), 3.07 (1H, s, 12-OH), 3.03 (1H, t,
H-4''eq), 2.72 (1H, dt, H-2), 2.64 (1H, H-3'), 2.42 (6H, s, 3'-NMe2),
2.36 (1H, d, H-2''b), 2.32 (1H, dt, H-10), 2.26 (1H, d, H-4''ax), 1.99
(1H, dt, H-4), 1.97-1.89 (2H, m, H-14b, H-7b), 1.83 (1H, d, H-4'b),
1.62-1.55 (2H, m, H-7a, H-2''a), 1.47 (1H, ddq, H-14a), 1.38 (3H, s,
6-Me), 1.29 (3H, d, 5''-Me), 1.25 (3H, s, 3''-Me), 1.23 (3H, d, 5'-Me),
1.21 (3H, d, 2-Me), 1.17 (3H, d, 10-Me), 1.16 (3H, d, 8-Me), 1.14 (3H, s,
12-Me), 1.11 (3H, d, 4-Me), 0.87 (3H, t, 15-Me). 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 175.8
(s, C-1), 174.3 (s, 8a-CONH), 137.4 (d, 6-OCH2CHCH2), 115.6 (t,
6-OCH2CHCH2), 102.8 (d, C-1'), 96.3 (d, C-1''), 81.2 (d, C-5), 79.7 (s,
C-6), 79.4 (d, C-3), 77.9 (d, C-4''), 77.1 (d, C-13), 74.2 (s, C-12),
72.8 (s, C-3''), 70.7 (d, C-11), 70.6 (d, C-2'), 68.7 (d, C-5'), 65.7 (t,
6-OCH2CHCH2), 65.6 (d, C-3'), 49.2 (q, 3''-OMe), 45.4 (d, C-2), 42.7 (t,
C-7), 42.2 (d, C-10), 41.5 (d, C-8), 41.3 (d, C-4), 40.3 (q, 3'-NMe2),
35.1 (t, C-2''), 29.4 (t, C-4'), 24.2 (q, 6-Me), 23.4 (q, 8-Me), 21.4 (q,
5'-Me), 21.4 (t, C-14), 21.1 (q, 3''-Me), 18.0 (q, 5''-Me), 16.1 (q,
12-Me), 15.5 (q, 2-Me), 10.8 (q, 15-Me), 9.8 (q, 4-Me), 9.6 (q, 10-Me).
Anal. (C40H72N2O13) C, H, N.
