$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: N-Methylamides IIa-IIe. A mixture of 1.5 mmol
of oxime, 5 ml of anhydrous ether and 5 ml of boron trifluoride etherate
was stirred for 1 h at room temperature. The precipitated crystals were
filtered off. N-Methylbenzamide (Ic). Yield 1.68 g (83%). mp 114-115°С
[9], Rf0.63. IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 3350 (NH), 1690 (C=O), 1600-1500
(C=Carom). 1Н NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 2.47 d (СН3NH, J 4.9 Hz), 7.06-7.14 m
(5Нarom), 9.60 br.s (NH).,
