$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 2-Arylcarbamoyl-4-phenyl-1,3-selenazoles (8); General
Procedure The ketoxime 7 (5.0 mmol) was dissolved in anhyd Et2O (30 mL)
and an excess of PCl5 (3.00 g) was subsequently added. The mixture was
refluxed with stirring for 30 min. Et2O was removed by distillation and
the residue was washed with H2O and recrystallized from EtOH to give 8.
2-Phenylcarbamoyl-4-phenyl-1,3-selenazole (8a) Yield: 1.30 g, 80%, yellow
needles. Yield: 1.30 g, 80%; yellow needles; mp 140-141 °C. IR (KBr): 880
(m) 901 (w), 1030 (w), 1066 (w), 1089 (w), 1198 (w), 1305 (s), 1575 (s),
1685 (s), 3080 (w) cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.02-7.94 (m, 10 H,
ArH), 8.32 (s, 2JSeH = 45.6 Hz, 1 H, 5-H,), 9.05 (br s, 1 H, NH). 13C NMR
(50 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 119.83 (5-C, Hetar), 124.77 (CH, Ar), 125.39 (CH,
Ar), 126.62 (CH, Ar), 128.48 (CH, Ar), 128.84 (CH, Ar), 129.15 (CH, Ar),
134.51 (Ar), 137.01 (Ar), 157.15 (4-C, Hetar), 158.53 (2-C, Hetar),
170.91 (C=O). MS (70 eV): m/z = 328 (56) [M+], 326 (29), 286 (11), 234
(3), 209 (14), 182 (20), 127 (5) 102 (100), 77 (10), 66 (19), 28 (2).
Anal. Calcd for C16H12N2OSe (327.23): C, 58.73; H, 3.70; N, 8.56. Found:
C, 58.81; H, 3.82; N, 8.72.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
