$DATUM 7787-60-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Beckmann
Rearrangement of oximes :- Benzophenone oxime 1 (R=Ph, 10 mmol) and
bismuth trichloride9 (12 mmol) were mixed together in an Erlenmeyer flask
and placed in a commercial microwave oven (operating at 2450 MHz
frequency) and irradiated for 8 minutes. The reaction mixture was allowed
to reach room temperature, treated with 20% sodium bicarbonate solution
and extracted with dichloromethane and dried over anhydrous sodium
sulphate. Removal of solvent and the residue on purification by column
chromatography on silica gel gave the corresponding benzanilide in 90%
yield and there was no evidence for. the formation of any deoximated
products. Similar treatment of 2-methyleyclohexanone and 1-tetralone
oximes gave the corresponding ring expanded rearranged products in 75-80%
yields as summerised in the table and their characteristics are recorded
here. 2i, yield 80%. mp 225-227 °C, Lit 12b mp 222-228°C. 1H NMR
2.10-3.60 (m., 6H, CH2); 7.10-7.30 (m, 5H, ArH & NH); IR. (KBr) 3270,
3200, 1635; MS m/e 147 (M+). Anal. Calcd. (found) for C12H12N2O: C, 71.98
(71.70); H, 6.04 (6.15); N, 13.99 (13.92).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microwave induced bismuth trichloride catalysed beckmann rearrangement of
oximes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Thakur, Ashim J.; Boruah, Anima; Prajapati, Dipak; Sandhu, Jagir S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2000), 30(12), 2105-2111

