$DATUM 5,7,7-Trimethyl-2-azabicyclo[4.1.1]oct-4-en-3-one (XIX) was obtained by
rearrangement of Z-isomer of oxime III in a 76% yield. mp 144-145°C
(publ.: mp 143-144°C [6]). IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 3280 (NH), 3060 (=C-H),
2955, 2925, 2865 (C-Haliph), 1645 (C=Oconjug.lactam), 1600 (C=Cconjug.).
1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 0.85 s (3H, 7-CH3-syn), 1.44 s (3H, 7-CH3-anti),
1.68 d.t (1H, H 7a , 2 J 10.2, 3 J7a',1 and 3 J7a',6 1.8 Hz), 1.85 d (3H,
5-CH3, 4 J 1.5 Hz), 2.22 d.t (1H, H 6 , 3 J6,8e' and 4 J6,1 5.6, 3 J6,8a'
1.8 Hz), 3.61 d.t (1H, H 1 , 3 J1,8e and 4 J1,6 5.6, 3 J1,8a' 1.8 Hz),
2.76 d.t (1H, H 8e , 2 J 10.2, 3 J1,8e and 3 J6,8e 5.6 Hz), 5.78 q (1H, H
4 , 4 JCH3 1.5 Hz). In the 1H NMR spectrum published in [6] were assigned
only the methyl groups signals and the signal of the olefin proton at C 4
atom. Mass spectrum, m/z (I rel, %):166 [M]+ (42), 151 [M - CH3] (19),
138 (7), 110 (100), 95, 84, 63, 43.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
