$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To the oxime 1 (0.4 mol) suspended in dry
ether (1500 ml) at 0°C is added gradually over 1-2 h, phosphorus
pentachloride (100.0 g, 0.48 mol) with efficient stirring and cooling.
After a further 2 h at 0°C, the mixture is stirred at ambient temperature
for the time given in Table 1. The clear solution is poured onto ice (∼ 1
kg) and carefully neutralised (pH 6-7) with aqueous 5 molar sodium
hydroxide solution maintaining a temperature of 0°C by ice addition. The
aqueous phase is further extracted with dichloromethane (3 × 150ml), the
combined organic phase is washed with water, dried with magnesium
sulphate, treated with charcoal, and evaporated. The residue is
triturated with petroleum ether (b.p. 40, 60°C), filtered, the filtered
product washed further with light petroleum ether, and recrystallised
from ethyl acetate/light petroleum ether (b.p, 60-80°C). Any tarry matter
is easily removed by filtration through a short alumina column with
chloroform/petroleum ether (1: 2). Product No: 2c, Reaction Time: 20 h,
Yield: 74%. m.p: 126 °C, Lit. m.p: (128°). I.R. (nujol)[cm-1]: νNH: 3200,
3250; νCO: 1660, 1650, 1H-N.M.R. (CDCl3)δ[ppm]: 7.27 (H-4); 7.21 (NH);
7.07 (H-3); 6.87 (H-3); 6.76 (H-4); J3,4: 4.2 Hz; 2.17 (COCH3),
13C-N.M.R. (CHCl3) or DMSO) δ[ppm]: 166.5 (CO); 139.9 (C-2); 130.1 (C-5);
125.6 (C-4); 109.8 (C-3); 21.9 (CH3).
